Subject: [M150] [turboshaft] Fix load elimination when map changes in a loop

Original change's description:
> [turboshaft] Fix load elimination when map changes in a loop
>
> When an object's map changes inside a loop (e.g. via an in-object property
> addition) or maps are wiped by a call/allocation,
> LateLoadEliminationAnalyzer's merge_maps must detect the discrepancy
> between the forward-edge snapshot and the backedge snapshot and trigger
> a loop revisit.
>
> Previously, merge_maps lacked a loop revisit check. Because alias
> analysis in pass 1 used the optimistic (stale) forward-edge map, stores
> through aliased pointers failed to invalidate loads, leaving memory
> snapshots identical on both edges and preventing merge_memory from
> detecting the need for a revisit.
>
> This CL adds the missing loop_needs_revisit check in merge_maps and
> cleans up the redundant predecessor map snapshot filtering.
>
